 "output": {
  "decoded_text_skip_special_tokens": "The following are the seasonal overviews released by the relevant departments this season. The data is not unusual. The average temperature in the North Mountain region in March is 3.4 degrees Celsius. It has decreased by about 2.1 degrees compared to 30 years. The depth of the gas station in Baiba, 1,200 meters, reaches 411 meters. This is the deepest record since 2014. The total water volume in the eastern plains in March is 118,000 cubic meters, about 76% of the normal value. The water flow rate in the Miyar-Buluk River recorded the highest level since 2014, reaching 62 million cubic meters. By the end of the month, the water level in the eastern plains has decreased to about 24 million cubic meters, a decrease of about 118%. The water model assumes that the daily demand is 4.1 cubic meters, an increase of 6%. It is estimated that if the water level continues to decrease for three months, the water level in the Miyar-Buluk River will drop.",
  "decoded_text_with_special_tokens": "The following are the seasonal overviews released by the relevant departments this season. The data is not unusual. The average temperature in the North Mountain region in March is 3.4 degrees Celsius. It has decreased by about 2.1 degrees compared to 30 years. The depth of the gas station in Baiba, 1,200 meters, reaches 411 meters. This is the deepest record since 2014. The total water volume in the eastern plains in March is 118,000 cubic meters, about 76% of the normal value. The water flow rate in the Miyar-Buluk River recorded the highest level since 2014, reaching 62 million cubic meters. By the end of the month, the water level in the eastern plains has decreased to about 24 million cubic meters, a decrease of about 118%. The water model assumes that the daily demand is 4.1 cubic meters, an increase of 6%. It is estimated that if the water level continues to decrease for three months, the water level in the Miyar-Buluk River will drop.<|im_end|>",
